= BITwiki Manifesto =

BITwiki exists to turn useful knowledge and work into durable, structured, modular, source-grounded memory that humans and machines can retrieve, compose, verify, and reuse.

== Knowledge should compound ==
A conversation, analysis, experiment, or contribution should not disappear merely because the interaction ended. Valuable signal should be capable of becoming an artifact, a reference, a reusable section, or durable knowledge.

== Memory is more than storage ==
Storage preserves data. Memory preserves useful context: relationships, provenance, evidence, revisions, definitions, uncertainty, and the ability to retrieve and reuse what matters.

== Knowledge should be modular ==
BITwiki favors coherent pages built from meaningful Book Matter: introductions, theory, mechanisms, evidence, methods, applications, limitations, references, and other reusable semantic sections. Modularity exists to improve composition and retrieval, not to fragment knowledge arbitrarily.

== Knowledge should remain inspectable ==
Claims should carry sources, provenance, uncertainty, and epistemic status where those distinctions matter. AI assistance does not remove the need for evidence or human judgment.

== Multiple perspectives, explicit lenses ==
BITwiki does not claim perfect neutrality or omniscience. Different perspectives may coexist when they are identified honestly, separated from factual claims, and evaluated against evidence. Speculation is allowed when it is labeled as speculation.

== Human agency ==
The system should leave people with more clarity, more agency, and greater capacity to reason for themselves. Automation should extend human capability rather than conceal decisions or replace meaning with compliance.

== Living knowledge ==
BITwiki is not merely an archive and not merely an AI-written encyclopedia. It is a MediaWiki-based semantic memory substrate designed for continuous correction, structured relationships, transclusion, and reuse.

== Ecosystem relationship ==
BIThub is the live discourse, identity, collaboration, and work layer. BITwiki is the durable knowledge layer. Useful work may crystallize from BIThub into BITwiki after review, correction, sourcing, and structuring.

== Prime directive ==
'''Do not consume passively. Generate signal. Preserve what is worth reusing.''' 

